# ── Under-development test files — NOT pushed to GitHub ──
# These spec files contain ONLY skipped test cases: their feature/screen or
# endpoint is not built yet, so every case is test.skip. Keeping them off
# GitHub stops the CI run from publishing a wall of "skipped/blocked" results
# to TestRail/CQM. They still live on disk (untracked) and are excluded from
# the local runner too (vitest `exclude` / playwright `testIgnore`).
#
# TO RE-ENABLE when a feature ships and its cases are un-skipped:
#   1. delete its line below
#   2. delete its line from the runner exclude list
#      (api-ts/vitest.config.ts `exclude` or frontend/playwright.config.ts `testIgnore`)
#   3. `git add` the file
#
# api-ts (no runnable cases — feature/endpoint/live-env not built):
api-ts/tests/admin.test.ts
api-ts/tests/audit.test.ts
api-ts/tests/auth.forgot-refresh-logout.test.ts
api-ts/tests/auth.login-setpw.test.ts
api-ts/tests/cache.test.ts
api-ts/tests/rbac.test.ts
api-ts/tests/tenant.test.ts
api-ts/tests/user.test.ts
api-ts/tests/vendor.test.ts
# frontend (screen not built):
frontend/tests/company-settings-access.spec.ts
frontend/tests/company-settings-edit.spec.ts
frontend/tests/company-settings-view.spec.ts
frontend/tests/user-management-create.spec.ts
frontend/tests/user-management-edit.spec.ts
frontend/tests/user-management-email.spec.ts
frontend/tests/user-management-status.spec.ts
